! mcp_bootstrap_p111.strap -- printed page 111, the INTERRUPT TABLE
! (SIT) slots 21 through 44.  docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.118,
! header READ AND NOT ASSUMED: the top line prints "TIME CLOCK
! 00054041  PUNID 11D11MCP  CARD ID DB000041  DIST. OF 3/01   3/01
! PAGE NUMBER 111", and the right-hand page header prints
! "LOCATION  215050", which is this page's first location.
!
! The CARD-ID PREFIX IS "DB" and that is not a guess: the two
! letters sit in this drum's O/C/D failure class, but
! docs/resuscitation_roadmap.md quotes "CARD ID DB000100" off PDF
! p.120 (printed p.113) from an independent rendering, and the D
! here has the straight vertical left stem and squared corners the
! round C of "DIST." in the same header does not.  (printed p.104's
! deck read its own prefix as "CB" and declined to claim it; this
! one is claimed.)
!
! FIFTY LINES, AND TWENTY-SIX CARDS.  The printed LINE column runs
! 1 to 50 with no gap and the page is blank below line 50.  The
! card-serial column runs DB000041 to DB000066 -- TWENTY-SIX
! serials for FIFTY lines, because MOST SERIALS APPEAR ON TWO
! CONSECUTIVE LINES.  That is not a scan artifact and it counts
! out exactly: line 1 (an SLC) is card 041 alone, lines 2+3 are
! card 042, line 4 (an SLC) is card 043 alone, and lines 5+6,
! 7+8, ... 49+50 are cards 044 through 066.
!     1 + 2 + 1 + 23*2 = 50 lines,  1+1+1+23 = 26 cards.
! So EACH INTERRUPT-SLOT CARD CARRIES BOTH HALF-WORD STATEMENTS OF
! ITS FULL WORD -- "SIC,S T IC" and "BD,SIPT+NN." -- and the
! listing prints one card as two lines.  Recorded as measured; the
! card-image mechanics are not needed by anything here.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT THE PAGE IS, AND A PRIMARY SOURCE THAT NAMES EVERY SYMBOL
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! C22-6728-1 7030 MCP System Analysis Guide, Interrupt Control
! (printed pp.12-46), printed p.12: MCP "keeps two 48-entry
! tables", the SIT -- "48 full word instructions of the form
! SIC,---; BD,---; one for each indicator 0 through 47" -- and the
! parallel SIPT.  THIS PAGE IS SIT SLOTS 21..44, two half words
! each.  Its own dispatch table (docs/ocr/C22-6728-1_7030_MCP_Sys_
! Analysis_Guide.txt line 1443, in the Interrupt Control chapter;
! THE PRINTED PAGE OF THAT TABLE IS NOT PINNED HERE -- the OCR
! carries no page marks -- so this is cited as an OCR line inside
! a chapter whose printed range IS pinned, not as a printed page)
! reads, column for column:
!
!     MASKABLE  TS(4)            STIC  SIPT+4.0   SINTO   JW LODE
!     All other maskable
!               (18, 20, 22-47)  STIC  SIPT+(indicator number)
!     I-O       (9-13)           STIC  SIPT+(indicator number)
!     IF        IF (21)          STIC  SIFAE
!
! That settles, by document and not by ink, every symbol on this
! page: S T IC is STIC, S IFA E is SIFAE, SIPT is SIPT, and the
! reason line 3 breaks the pattern is that SLOT 21 IS THE IF
! (instruction fetch) INTERRUPT, which goes to the IF ANALYZER
! instead of the parallel table.  The page's own comments agree in
! English: line 1 "-TO PLACE IF INTERRUPT INSTRUCTION IN" and line
! 3 "-IFA INTERRUPT INSTRUCTION".  SIFAE is also in the Guide's
! named-routine list for Interrupt Control, recorded in
! docs/archival_inventory_notes.md:130 ("...RVFCSG etc/SIFAE/SIFAD/
! MTC1/...").
!
! Line 1    SLC,S IT+21.0   -- origin to SIT slot 21.
! Line 2    SIC,S T IC      -- store the IC.
! Line 3    BD,S IFA E      -- branch disabled to the IF analyzer.
! Line 4    SLC, S IT+22.   -- origin to SIT slot 22.
! Lines 5-50  twenty-three more slots, 22 through 44, each
!             "SIC,ST IC" at word.00 and "BD,SIPT+NN." at word.40.
! No NAME is printed on any of the fifty lines, no SYN, no DD, no
! comment card.  The page is forty-eight half-word instructions
! and two SLC cards.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> THERE IS NOTHING FOR !SYM TO LOOK AT, AND THAT IS CORRECT.
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! The NAME column is EMPTY on all fifty lines, so this page defines
! no symbol.  The four names below are SYN STAND-INS FOR EXTERNALS
! that this deck declares itself; writing "!SYM SIT 215023.00"
! would check this deck's own declaration against itself and prove
! nothing.  None is written.  printed p.104's deck has the mirror
! case -- twenty-three !SYM and no !CHECK -- and says so for the
! same reason.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE FOUR EXTERNALS, AND THE EVIDENCE CLASS OF EACH
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> ALL FOUR WERE READ IN docs/ocr/MCP_Mar63_001-249.txt AND NOT
! RE-RENDERED. <<<  printed p.103's deck established that OCR-only
! evidence is a weaker class than a render and must be labelled;
! every witness below is OCR-only, and each OCR line's printed page
! was resolved from the file's own "===== PDF page N =====" marks
! with the verified +7 offset.
!
!   SIT    215023.00  -- ALREADY CARRIED BY A LANDED DECK.
!       decks/mcp_bootstrap_p103.strap:290 declares
!       "SIT SYN,(8)215023.0" off printed p.110's label
!       ("S IT  SIC,YMFIC" at 215023.00) and printed p.175's
!       "SIT($4)".  THAT SPELLING IS REUSED HERE DELIBERATELY
!       rather than invented, per the house rule to prefer a
!       spelling another page already uses.
!       AND THIS PAGE IS AN INDEPENDENT CHECK OF IT: line 1's
!       "SLC,S IT+21.0" prints 215050.00, and 0o215023 + 21
!       words (0o25) = 0o215050.  All forty-eight of this page's
!       locations hang off that one number.
!
!   SIPT   215103.00  -- DEFINED ON THE NEXT PRINTED PAGE, and
!       corroborated four more times:
!         printed p.112 line 7  "S IPT  BEW," at 215103.00, the
!             DEFINING LABEL, comment "-BASE ADDRESS OF PARALLEL
!             INTERRUPT T[ABLE]"   (OCR line 5870)
!         printed p.112, the SLC row below it: "SLC,SIPT+4.0"
!             prints 215107.00  (that row's LINE number is
!             garbled in the OCR and is not claimed)
!         printed p.144        "B,SIPT+4.0" prints 215107.10
!             (a plain B prints target + 8 bits)
!         printed p.130        "V-I,2,SIPT+1.0" prints 215104.05
!         printed p.143        "LVI,$1,SIPT+18.0" prints 215125.03
!       All five give 0o215103.  NOT a tautology.
!
!   STIC   215265.00  -- its defining row is printed p.116, which
!       prints 215265.00 against "000000.00+ ... VF,0" with the
!       NAME garbled by the OCR; the row above it is "S UPPER" and
!       the row below "S IC PP VF,0" at 215323.00, so the shape is
!       right.  THE ADDRESS DOES NOT REST ON THAT ROW: printed
!       pp.117, 127, 136, 141, 143, 144 and 175 print
!       operands "LV,$0,STIC" / "SVA,$0,STIC" / "SIC,STIC" with the
!       half word 215265.xx, agreeing digit for digit.  NOT a
!       tautology.
!
!   SIFAE  215471.00  -- THE WEAK ONE, AND IT IS SAID PLAINLY.
!       Its spelling is settled by C22-6728-1 above.  Its ADDRESS
!       has exactly ONE witness outside this page: a row of
!       printed p.175 (its LINE number is garbled in the OCR),
!       on a page that prints a SECOND COPY of this same SIT
!       pattern at 220644..220647 and whose "BD,SIFAE" at
!       220645.40 prints "215471.04 00" -- the same target this
!       page's line 3 prints at 215050.40.  That OCR row is badly
!       garbled in its text column ("FFC((((( (#U#C#C#N BOYSIFAED")
!       though its two octal fields are clean.  IF THAT WITNESS
!       DOES NOT HOLD, LINE 3 IS A TAUTOLOGY.  It was not
!       re-rendered.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> BOTH SLC CARDS ARE REDUNDANT RE-ORIGINS, AND THAT COSTS THE
! JOIN. <<<
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! printed p.110's last row is line 48, "215047.40  215127.04 00
! BD,SIPT+20." -- a half word, so the location counter ARRIVES at
! 215050.00, which is exactly where line 1's "SLC,S IT+21.0" sends
! it.  Line 4's "SLC, S IT+22." lands on 215051.00, where line 3's
! half word had already left it.  Neither SLC moves anything.
!
! printed p.104's hazard applies: AN SLC CANNOT DISAGREE WITH THE
! ARRIVING COUNTER, IT OVERRIDES IT SILENTLY.  So this page does
! NOT test that printed p.110 lands against it; when p.110's deck
! exists, that join must be compared by hand.
!
! One thing is better here than in p.104's case and is worth
! saying: both SLCs are written SYMBOLICALLY, "SIT+21.0" and
! "SIT+22.", EXACTLY AS PRINTED -- no hard octal literal was
! substituted.  So the page's whole address chain is tied to SIT's
! external value instead of asserting an address, and if SIT were
! wrong by one word every one of the forty-eight checked locations
! would miss.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT THE FORTY-EIGHT !CHECK ROWS ACTUALLY CHECK
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Forty-eight rows, but NOT forty-eight independent facts:
!
!  * 24 rows print "215265.00 80" -- ONE fact (STIC = 215265.00,
!    plus the SIC half-word encoding) repeated twenty-four times.
!  * 23 rows print "2151NN.04 00" for BD,SIPT+22. .. BD,SIPT+44.
!    These ARE twenty-three distinct checks, because the operand
!    is written in DECIMAL and the location prints in OCTAL and
!    every one of the twenty-three maps differently:
!      +22. -> 215131   (22 dec = 26 oct)
!      +28. -> 215137   (28 dec = 34 oct)
!      +29.0-> 215140   the octal carry
!      +36. -> 215147
!      +37. -> 215150   the next carry
!      +44. -> 215157   (44 dec = 54 oct)
!    That decimal-to-octal word arithmetic at twenty-three points,
!    against a base address read off five other printed pages, is
!    this page's real check surface.
!  * 1 row prints "215471.04 00" for BD,S IFA E -- see SIFAE above.
!  * ALL 48 LOCATIONS rest on SIT = 215023.00 through line 1.
!
! The BD encoding itself is checked forty-eight ways over: a BD to
! word W prints "W.04 00", which is what printed p.38 lines 12 and
! 17 print and what printed p.103 line 43 prints for SDISIC+.32.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE GLYPHS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THIS PAGE OPENS ROUND GLYPHS CONSTANTLY and proves it in its own
! column heading, which prints "LOCATICN" for LOCATION, and in its
! header, which prints "TIME CLCCK 00054041" and "DIST. CF 3/C1".
! So shape alone decides nothing, which is why C22-6728-1 is cited
! above rather than a zoom.
!
! EVERY FIELD THIS DECK READS IS OCTAL, and a round glyph in an
! octal field is a 0 with certainty because C is not an octal
! digit.  At 900 dpi line 2's location renders "215C50.CO", line 4's
! "215C51.CC *", line 35's "215C7C.CC", line 8's binary
! "215132.04 CO", line 16's "215136.C4 CO".  Every one of those C's
! is a 0 and is read as a 0.
!
! THE TWO BYTES ARE SETTLED ON WHAT PRODUCED THEM, not on the
! page's ink:
!   * "80" on the SIC rows.  The 8 prints with both bowls closed at
!     900 dpi, and it is the byte that printed p.113 prints for
!     "SIC,WINTOR" (216371.40 80, quoted in
!     docs/resuscitation_roadmap.md off an independent render) and
!     that printed pp.119/169/173/193 print for "SIC,SDISIC".
!     B0 is excluded by the instruction, not by the stroke.
!   * "00" on the BD rows.  A BD to word W compiles "W.04 00";
!     decks/mcp_bootstrap_p38.strap records "002422.04 00" for
!     "BD,S CA6" and "002502.04 00" for "BD,S BRK8", and
!     decks/mcp_bootstrap_p103.strap records "217452.04 00" for
!     "BD,SDISIC+.32".  The assembler reproduces all forty-eight.
!
! THE FOUR OPERANDS THAT PRINT A TRAILING ".0" -- lines 20, 22, 24
! and 26, "BD,SIPT+29.0" through "BD,SIPT+32.0", where the other
! nineteen print a bare "+NN." -- ARE TRANSCRIBED AS PRINTED.  Two
! of the four render their 0 open ("+29.C", "+31.C"); that field is
! a DECIMAL bit offset and cannot hold a C either, so all four are
! ".0".  A ".0" bit offset is bit-identical to no bit offset and
! none of the four changes a compiled bit; the difference is in the
! card, not in the machine.
!
! B vs 8 and C vs D gave no trouble: the only letters this page
! prints in a checked field are the "8" of "80", and the only
! letters in a NAME are in SIPT, STIC and SIFAE, all three settled
! by document above.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! SPELLING VARIANTS -- ONE SYMBOL, FOUR PRINTINGS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! BLANKS INSIDE SYMBOL NAMES ARE DROPPED, as on every page since
! p.2.  The STATEMENT column prints the SAME operand four ways and
! they are one symbol:
!     line  2  "SIC,S T IC"    lines 5-18, 27-50  "SIC,ST IC"
!     lines 19-25 (odd)  "SIC,STIC"
! and likewise "SLC,S IT+21.0" / "SLC, S IT+22." for SIT and
! "BD,S IFA E" for SIFAE against the unspaced "BD,SIPT+NN.".
! The inter-word spacing is card column position and is not load-
! bearing; it is recorded in the listing block below exactly as
! read and written one way in the code.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! LISTING MARKS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Every one of the fifty line numbers carries an asterisk right
! after it ("1*", "50*"); that is the ordinary column, as on
! printed pp.99/104, and is not a mark.  FOUR ROWS CARRY A SECOND
! ASTERISK AFTER THE LOCATION -- lines 1, 4, 27 and 50, e.g.
! "215077.40 *" -- the same mark printed pp.3/37/38/39/88/97/98/
! 103/104 carry.  Lines 1 and 4 are the two SLC cards; lines 27 and
! 50 are ordinary BD/SIC rows and nothing distinguishes them from
! their neighbours.  RECORDED, NOT EXPLAINED.  No mark changes a
! compiled bit and none is checked.
!
! (printed p.112 carries the same mark on its own
! "SLC,SIPT+4.0", which is consistent with the mark attaching to
! an SLC -- but lines 27 and 50 here are not SLCs, so that cannot
! be the whole rule.  printed p.111 line 27 is the 27th line and
! printed p.104's marked row was its line 6, so it is not a fixed
! line either.)
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHERE THE PAGE SITS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! FIRST 215050.00 (line 1, and line 2 is the first row to spend
! storage), LAST 215077.40 (line 50).  Twenty-four full words,
! forty-eight half words, contiguous: nothing on this page skips a
! bit.  printed p.110 ends at 215047.40 and printed p.112 opens at
! 215100.00 with "SIC,ST IC" and continues the SAME table with
! slots 45, 46 and 47 at 215100.40 / 215101.40 / 215102.40, then
! defines S IPT itself at 215103.00.  So the chain p.110 -> p.111
! -> p.112 is contiguous.
!
! THIS IS THE SECOND ASSEMBLY -- printed p.99 line 11's
! "SLC,(8)215000." origin, outside the TAIL,(2)G block that
! printed p.2 opened and printed p.98 line 37 closed.  Names here
! may legitimately repeat names defined in pp.2-98 at different
! addresses.  NONE OF THIS PAGE'S FOUR NAMES COLLIDES with any
! landed deck: SIT is already declared with this same value in
! decks/mcp_bootstrap_p103.strap, and SIPT, STIC and SIFAE appear
! in no deck in decks/ at all.

! ---- externals, with the printed page each value was read on -------
! All four read in docs/ocr/MCP_Mar63_001-249.txt, not re-rendered.
SIT     SYN, (8)215023.0             ! p.110 label; p.175 SIT($4);
                                      ! already in p.103's deck
SIPT    SYN, (8)215103.0             ! p.112 line 7 DEFINES "S IPT";
                                      ! pp.112,130,143,144 references
STIC    SYN, (8)215265.0             ! p.116 definition row; operand
                                      ! on pp.117,127,136,141,143,
                                      ! 144,175
SIFAE   SYN, (8)215471.0             ! ONE witness, p.175 "BD,SIFAE"
                                      ! -> 215471.04.  See above.

! ---- SIT slot 21 -- the IF (instruction fetch) interrupt -----------
        SLC, SIT+21.0                ! line  1 -TO PLACE IF INTERRUPT
                                      !          INSTRUCTION IN
        SIC, STIC                    ! line  2
        BD, SIFAE                    ! line  3 -IFA INTERRUPT
                                      !          INSTRUCTION

! ---- SIT slots 22..44 -- the parallel-interrupt-table slots --------
        SLC, SIT+22.                 ! line  4
        SIC, STIC                    ! line  5
        BD, SIPT+22.                 ! line  6
        SIC, STIC                    ! line  7
        BD, SIPT+23.                 ! line  8
        SIC, STIC                    ! line  9
